1
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,367
Ward One has privileges,

2
00:00:12,367 --> 00:00:15,200
endless supplies, and patience
with food check marks.

3
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,067
Thankfully, George has a friend.

4
00:00:19,133 --> 00:00:21,233
So Noa, Noa, Noa.

5
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,067
I was thinking maybe
we should hang out sometime.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:25,467
Dinner?

7
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:26,967
Something spicy.

8
00:00:27,467 --> 00:00:28,667
Um, food-food?

9
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:31,267
[CHUCKLES] I'm just eating
whatever fits in my pocket.

10
00:00:31,267 --> 00:00:34,467
Well, I am known for my
protein-forward pesto chicken.

11
00:00:35,033 --> 00:00:37,133
Wait, w-what are you doing?

12
00:00:38,533 --> 00:00:39,433
Oh, um...

13
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:40,600
Yeah, you got to train
the obliques.

14
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:42,067
[GROANS]

15
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:43,733
Side plank the soul.

16
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:46,567
Uh, definitely a yellow flag.

17
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:49,700
So, you want to touch this?

18
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,133
No, no. [CHUCKLES]

19
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:52,233
Don't worry.

20
00:00:52,233 --> 00:00:53,233
Most people ask.

21
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:54,767
You're lucky.

22
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:56,433
[CHUCKLES] Red flag! Red flag!

23
00:00:57,267 --> 00:00:58,233
What?

24
00:00:59,167 --> 00:01:01,767
So, uh, dinner? Thursday?

25
00:01:02,233 --> 00:01:04,233
Oh, I'm allergic...

26
00:01:04,633 --> 00:01:05,500
To food?

27
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,467
To everything
that just happened.

28
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,567
JC's coming for Ward Five.

29
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:13,800
You're going to be busy.

30
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:15,167
[CHUCKLES]

31
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:16,600
It's the perks of Ward One.

32
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:17,533
[SMOOCHES]

33
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:25,033
I'd do him.

34
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:26,333
[GROANS]

35
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:28,800
This JC thing?

36
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,067
That's trouble.

37
00:01:36,533 --> 00:01:38,067
Excuse me.

38
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:40,133
Back in my time,
guys would sing for me

39
00:01:40,133 --> 00:01:42,067
and ask for the
parents' blessings.

40
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,333
[CHUCKLES] You should've
hit him where it counts!

41
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:46,300
- Is that how Mr. Tess got you?
- No!

42
00:01:46,567 --> 00:01:47,633
Eyes forward, Noa.

43
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:49,267
You look like you're talking
to yourself again.

44
00:01:49,733 --> 00:01:50,667
Got any intel?

45
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:53,233
Yeah, the Latino ghost
heard whispers,

46
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:54,667
joint commission, our Ward.

47
00:01:54,667 --> 00:01:55,667
I didn't hear anything.

48
00:01:55,667 --> 00:01:57,800
Uh, we have a lot of
gossips floating around.

49
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,333
That's impossible!

50
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:01,633
We've hit all of our marks.

51
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,167
JC's no joke, dear.

52
00:02:05,533 --> 00:02:07,433
They don't just do
unannounced visits.

53
00:02:07,433 --> 00:02:14,400
- [WIND HOWLING]
- [LIGHTS FLICKERING]

54
00:02:15,867 --> 00:02:17,667
D-Did you feel that?

55
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,567
Okay, that's new.

56
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:22,100
What's wrong?

57
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,167
I'm okay, dear.

58
00:02:25,733 --> 00:02:26,633
Go see Jane.

59
00:02:26,633 --> 00:02:33,133
- [WIND HOWLING]
- [LIGHTS FLICKERING]

60
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:34,367
[JANE] Relax.

61
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:37,333
I would've been flagged
if they were on site.

62
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:38,700
Are you sure?

63
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,333
Is there not someone
we can call?

64
00:02:41,267 --> 00:02:43,700
We all have our connections,
Noa.

65
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:48,800
You just have to know
who bought who dinner.

66
00:02:48,833 --> 00:02:50,467
[DIALING, LINE RINGING]

67
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,367
Hey, you.

68
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:54,567
It's me.

69
00:02:55,433 --> 00:02:57,567
I know. I miss you too.

70
00:02:58,733 --> 00:03:01,500
No, I can't. I'm married now.

71
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:06,233
Anywho, quick ask.

72
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:08,933
Is JC supposed to be
at the hospital today?

73
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:10,567
I know it's a silly question.

74
00:03:10,567 --> 00:03:14,933
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

75
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:16,667
What do you mean
their flight was delayed?

76
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,300
Alright everyone,
we have a few hours,

77
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:23,833
but that's more than
enough time.

78
00:03:23,833 --> 00:03:25,333
I mean,
look at what we've built.

79
00:03:25,333 --> 00:03:26,900
Now let's show them
who we are.

80
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:28,333
Okay, throw the SOPs at me.

81
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:31,633
I will skim them emotionally
and somehow know everything.

82
00:03:31,633 --> 00:03:33,700
Zero OSHA violations, people.

83
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,833
Fix, repair, tape all signage.

84
00:03:35,833 --> 00:03:38,467
All rooms will have flowers.
They're sponsored by me.

85
00:03:38,467 --> 00:03:40,367
Don't use your phones.
HIPAA matters.

86
00:03:40,367 --> 00:03:41,567
Dust, I kill you.

87
00:03:41,567 --> 00:03:42,600
Crap, I'm nice.

88
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,333
Here's 20, clean more.

89
00:03:44,333 --> 00:03:45,733
(In Latin)
Talk to all the ghosts,

90
00:03:45,733 --> 00:03:47,200
I don't want
any hauntings today.

91
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,833
And you, don't you have
anything to do?

92
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:49,933
We got this, Noa.

93
00:03:49,933 --> 00:03:51,500
Has anyone seen Grim?

94
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,667
He's scheduled today.

95
00:03:52,667 --> 00:03:54,367
No, I haven't seen him.

96
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,767
Do you need help
with medication?

97
00:03:55,767 --> 00:03:57,233
Oh! I'm okay. Thank you.

98
00:03:58,933 --> 00:04:00,933
Oh! Just make sure
those records are up to date.

99
00:04:00,933 --> 00:04:01,933
- Okay.
- On it.

100
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,800
Let's take a breath

101
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:07,267
before anyone accuses
anyone of anything.

102
00:04:07,267 --> 00:04:10,367
You were there!
You heard him make that threat.

103
00:04:10,367 --> 00:04:12,333
I will not have you
walking around here

104
00:04:12,333 --> 00:04:14,333
besmirching my name, Jane.

105
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:15,767
Besmirching?

106
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,467
[PAPERS SCATTER]

107
00:04:17,467 --> 00:04:19,467
I got you besmirching
right here, mother--

108
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,767
- Oh, hey-- Security!
- What you got, Walt?

109
00:04:21,767 --> 00:04:23,333
- What's up?
- Hold on.

110
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:26,433
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

111
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:30,567
[MOP THUDS]

112
00:04:30,867 --> 00:04:31,867
They're here.

113
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:33,600
Early.

114
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:34,933
Are we dead?

115
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:38,467
Looks like Mariah Carey
threw up Christmas in here.

116
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,767
I didn't raise a coward.

117
00:04:41,467 --> 00:04:42,733
[EXHALES] We got this.

118
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:49,267
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:04:49,267 --> 00:04:50,600
Complaint 39.

120
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,433
Requirement for staff
to communicate

121
00:04:52,433 --> 00:04:53,800
in a non-English language.

122
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,367
What? No, I would never.

123
00:04:55,367 --> 00:04:56,367
Excuse me.

124
00:04:56,367 --> 00:04:57,367
Actually...

125
00:04:57,367 --> 00:04:59,333
per Joint Commission
communication standard

126
00:04:59,333 --> 00:05:02,367
RI.01.01.03,

127
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,433
staff are allowed
to speak another language

128
00:05:03,433 --> 00:05:06,300
if it helps facilitate
patient comprehension.

129
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:08,633
(In Filipino)
So, thank you very much!

130
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,300
You speak Filipino?

131
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:12,700
Ros forces me to learn it
because I get lost a lot.

132
00:05:13,633 --> 00:05:14,600
[GASPS]

133
00:05:17,433 --> 00:05:18,367
Noted.

134
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,000
- [SPRAY HISSES]
- Trust me, darling.

135
00:05:25,933 --> 00:05:27,300
Those will kill you.

136
00:05:39,567 --> 00:05:41,367
Do you like the flowers?

137
00:05:41,367 --> 00:05:42,400
They're fresh.

138
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,067
Hello?

139
00:05:49,533 --> 00:05:50,600
Did you hear me?

140
00:05:55,633 --> 00:06:00,000
Complaint 5517.

141
00:06:00,767 --> 00:06:04,367
Potential contamination risk
due to unsecured

142
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:07,600
open beverage on
a patient care surface.

143
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:11,567
I literally just walked
through this room!

144
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:13,733
Get the EVS!

145
00:06:13,933 --> 00:06:16,700
I'm not going to get cited
just because of a cup.

146
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,400
I'm going to post about this.

147
00:06:22,767 --> 00:06:24,567
That wasn't there earlier.

148
00:06:26,833 --> 00:06:31,867
- [WIND HOWLING]
- [EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

149
00:06:31,867 --> 00:06:33,333
Who are you?

150
00:06:33,533 --> 00:06:39,733
[MUSIC TURNS SUSPENSEFUL]

151
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:41,033
- [MUSIC STOPS]
- [BEEPS]

152
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,300
Hello.

153
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,633
I'm trying to pull up
the patient complaints

154
00:06:44,633 --> 00:06:45,567
for Ward Five.

155
00:06:45,567 --> 00:06:47,833
The dashboard
isn't showing anything.

156
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:50,400
[WOMAN]<i> And what seems
</i> to be the issue?

157
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,500
It's blank.

158
00:06:51,733 --> 00:06:53,667
Zero complaints for months.

159
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:58,100
There are no complaints.
Why the hell is JC here?

160
00:06:58,533 --> 00:06:59,567
<i> Please hold.</i>

161
00:06:59,567 --> 00:07:03,433
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:07:03,433 --> 00:07:04,733
[LINE DISCONNECTS]

163
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:05,733
Hello?

164
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,100
Hello?

165
00:07:09,467 --> 00:07:11,867
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

166
00:07:11,867 --> 00:07:14,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

167
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,067
[EXHALES]

168
00:07:23,633 --> 00:07:25,433
It smells weird in here.

169
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:28,467
Strawberries.

170
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:32,467
I need to verify an item
reported on Rack 7B.

171
00:07:32,467 --> 00:07:33,400
Hmm.

172
00:07:41,567 --> 00:07:42,800
Expired.

173
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,067
[WRITING]

174
00:07:52,633 --> 00:07:54,433
That wasn't supposed
to be there.

175
00:07:54,733 --> 00:07:57,433
I didn't have time to finish
checking all the cabinets.

176
00:07:58,833 --> 00:08:00,467
[SIGHS] This is all my fault.

177
00:08:00,467 --> 00:08:02,033
I should have let the CNA help.

178
00:08:02,567 --> 00:08:03,533
No, Noa.

179
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:05,133
Someone told her.

180
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:13,533
[GRUNTS]

181
00:08:13,533 --> 00:08:17,067
This is where it all
began for you, isn't it?

182
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:21,600
What are you?

183
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:26,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

184
00:08:26,167 --> 00:08:28,867
How many breaths
did you try to steal

185
00:08:28,867 --> 00:08:31,133
before your body just...

186
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:32,800
gave up?

187
00:08:33,233 --> 00:08:37,100
Whatever you are,
let me help my daughter.

188
00:08:38,767 --> 00:08:40,767
Do forgive my bedside manner.

189
00:08:41,867 --> 00:08:45,933
My presence means
the message is overdue.

190
00:08:46,967 --> 00:08:48,633
You're an Archangel?

191
00:08:49,233 --> 00:08:50,833
Clever girl.

192
00:08:51,767 --> 00:08:54,200
You do rise marginally
above the rabble.

193
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,167
Where's Grim?

194
00:08:58,700 --> 00:09:01,133
You remember what he told you
a few months back?

195
00:09:03,233 --> 00:09:07,533
<i>Every rule shattered
demands its due.</i>

196
00:09:07,833 --> 00:09:09,967
<i>That's how it works.
That's the truth.</i>

197
00:09:10,733 --> 00:09:11,900
<i> Then I'll pay it.</i>

198
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:15,233
Because we allow it.

199
00:09:15,933 --> 00:09:17,733
You're not an angel.

200
00:09:17,733 --> 00:09:18,733
You're a demon!

201
00:09:18,733 --> 00:09:19,967
Demon! Demon!

202
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:22,867
[MUFFLED SPEAKING]

203
00:09:22,867 --> 00:09:24,967
Do be careful
with my feelings, darling.

204
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
He has permitted patience.

205
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,700
I'm not.

206
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,533
But you...

207
00:09:34,267 --> 00:09:35,600
I know you.

208
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:39,533
Hard hands.

209
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,933
Harsher words.

210
00:09:43,033 --> 00:09:44,633
I love yous.

211
00:09:45,067 --> 00:09:48,633
Rationed like wartime sugar.

212
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:52,633
It's no mystery
she's glued to you.

213
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,833
Children crave what
they're starved of.

214
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:59,100
[MUFFLED SPEAKING]

215
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,133
- [MUFFLED SPEAKING]
- Hmm.

216
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:02,233
Don't pout, Tessy Tess.

217
00:10:03,733 --> 00:10:07,167
All those secrets you hoarded.

218
00:10:08,667 --> 00:10:09,933
You fed her.

219
00:10:09,933 --> 00:10:11,333
You clothed her.

220
00:10:12,933 --> 00:10:14,667
Yet you never told her.

221
00:10:16,733 --> 00:10:18,833
[MUFFLED SPEAKING]

222
00:10:19,367 --> 00:10:21,233
And you had decades.

223
00:10:21,233 --> 00:10:26,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

224
00:10:26,767 --> 00:10:28,233
[MUSIC FADES]

225
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,200
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

226
00:10:34,833 --> 00:10:35,833
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

227
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:37,100
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

228
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:41,900
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

229
00:10:52,733 --> 00:10:55,300
[ARTHUR] Yo! N-n-n-Noa!

230
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:57,100
Could this day get any worse?

231
00:10:58,800 --> 00:10:59,933
[GRUNTING]

232
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:02,167
Told you they were coming.

233
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,733
How did you know?

234
00:11:04,733 --> 00:11:06,733
Oh, dude.
Let me tell you over dinner.

235
00:11:06,733 --> 00:11:07,833
You still allergic?

236
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:09,400
What?

237
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:10,767
[ARTHUR] To Thursday?

238
00:11:10,767 --> 00:11:11,767
To dates?

239
00:11:11,767 --> 00:11:12,867
With me?

240
00:11:13,667 --> 00:11:14,800
[GEORGE] Hey.

241
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:16,833
What's going on here?

242
00:11:16,833 --> 00:11:18,667
[ARTHUR] Oh, bro.

243
00:11:18,667 --> 00:11:19,700
It's all good. It's gravy.

244
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:22,100
We're just scheduling
our date for Thursday.

245
00:11:22,833 --> 00:11:23,933
[GRUNTS]

246
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:28,733
God, what?
Even your jaw's ripped?

247
00:11:28,733 --> 00:11:29,900
Oh, yeah.

248
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,800
Thirty minutes a day
of chewing gum.

249
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,067
- Okay.
- Straight sets.

250
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:35,667
George, don't give me
any more problems today.

251
00:11:35,667 --> 00:11:37,200
I'm not. I just...

252
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:40,800
He was smiling weird
and you looked sad and...

253
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,167
I got scared.

254
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,400
[ARTHUR] You do have great
wrist alignment though.

255
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:45,400
Yeah.

256
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:46,467
- Thanks, man.
- Okay.

257
00:11:46,467 --> 00:11:48,267
Stop complimenting violence!

258
00:11:48,467 --> 00:11:49,733
And...

259
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:51,733
you're on for Thursday.

260
00:11:52,067 --> 00:11:53,467
Ha! Yes!

261
00:11:53,467 --> 00:11:55,167
Stoked. You're going
to love my pesto.

262
00:11:55,167 --> 00:11:57,267
You got a great swing, buddy.
[CHUCKLES]

263
00:11:59,833 --> 00:12:00,967
[SCOFFS]

264
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:02,867
What was that about?

265
00:12:03,133 --> 00:12:04,267
Intel.

266
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:06,867
I hate secrets.

267
00:12:08,967 --> 00:12:10,800
Today was a disaster, huh?

268
00:12:11,233 --> 00:12:12,333
Pretty much.

269
00:12:13,133 --> 00:12:14,333
You okay?

270
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,133
[NOA] You don't strike me
as the violent type.

271
00:12:18,233 --> 00:12:19,800
Shouldn't have been
hitting on you.

272
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,067
[NOA CHUCKLES FAINTLY]

273
00:12:21,067 --> 00:12:23,233
I just mean, you don't deserve
to get cornered

274
00:12:23,233 --> 00:12:25,033
on top of everything else today.

275
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:27,600
Come on.

276
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,967
Let's head inside.
We need to post-mortem.

277
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:43,967
[JAY] Hi.

278
00:12:47,067 --> 00:12:49,033
I got your messages...

279
00:12:49,933 --> 00:12:51,733
your emails...

280
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:53,900
and screenshots.

281
00:12:54,167 --> 00:12:56,767
We don't get the results of
the visit for a couple of days.

282
00:12:56,767 --> 00:12:57,900
Maybe they'll pass.

283
00:12:58,833 --> 00:13:00,800
You're not that stupid, Jay.

284
00:13:01,767 --> 00:13:03,233
Noa's only had
a couple of months

285
00:13:03,233 --> 00:13:06,233
to whip this place into shape,
and she's done a good job.

286
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:07,767
[JAY] Lady, don't do that.

287
00:13:07,767 --> 00:13:09,067
Do what?

288
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:12,800
I've had your back since
day one, and you know this.

289
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,733
You don't understand.

290
00:13:14,933 --> 00:13:15,967
I do.

291
00:13:16,167 --> 00:13:17,867
We're in the business of caring.

292
00:13:18,067 --> 00:13:19,967
It's okay to care.

293
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:26,233
When I was a surgical resident,
we had a boy who was gone.

294
00:13:27,033 --> 00:13:28,367
My attending said it.

295
00:13:29,167 --> 00:13:30,300
He wouldn't survive.

296
00:13:30,867 --> 00:13:31,867
But I was stubborn.

297
00:13:31,867 --> 00:13:33,933
This isn't about you.

298
00:13:33,933 --> 00:13:35,067
[JAY] Let me finish.

299
00:13:36,567 --> 00:13:38,533
After the first operation,
he sank.

300
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,467
So I rolled him back in.

301
00:13:41,167 --> 00:13:42,300
Scalpel.

302
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:44,200
Suction.

303
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,133
Stitch.

304
00:13:47,467 --> 00:13:49,800
I cut until the anatomy frayed.

305
00:13:50,067 --> 00:13:52,433
I cut until his skin curled
like paper.

306
00:13:53,567 --> 00:13:54,867
So what?

307
00:13:55,433 --> 00:13:57,000
You'd let him die?

308
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:59,433
At some point you
have to ask yourself,

309
00:13:59,433 --> 00:14:01,000
when is caring too much?

310
00:14:01,867 --> 00:14:04,233
This was targeted!

311
00:14:05,167 --> 00:14:06,533
[JAY] Even if it was.

312
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:10,300
If you keep pouring blood
in a limb you can't save...

313
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,300
you'll bleed out the whole body.

314
00:14:18,233 --> 00:14:19,367
Judas.

315
00:14:19,933 --> 00:14:26,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

316
00:14:41,933 --> 00:14:48,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

317
00:15:03,967 --> 00:15:10,933
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,900
[GEORGE] Hey.

319
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,267
We almost finished taking down

320
00:15:25,267 --> 00:15:27,067
the decorations
they complained about.

321
00:15:32,933 --> 00:15:34,067
[SIGHS]

322
00:15:35,133 --> 00:15:36,500
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

323
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,933
They didn't wait
for the full report.

324
00:15:52,033 --> 00:15:54,167
This was already decided.

325
00:15:54,967 --> 00:15:57,567
The board is closing Ward Five.

326
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,567
Like for renovation?

327
00:16:00,033 --> 00:16:01,167
[JANE] Closure.

328
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:05,267
Patients to be reassigned
within 48 hours.

329
00:16:05,267 --> 00:16:06,500
- Staff--
- No!

330
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,633
They can't just transfer us.

331
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:12,133
This is the only work
I've ever actually enjoyed.

332
00:16:12,133 --> 00:16:13,500
Or tolerated.

333
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,700
I'd be crying if
my tear ducts worked.

334
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:17,367
I'm fired, aren't I?

335
00:16:17,367 --> 00:16:18,933
That's impossible.

336
00:16:19,433 --> 00:16:22,267
They can't fire the person
holding it together.

337
00:16:22,667 --> 00:16:25,267
I've met a lot of
divas and directors,

338
00:16:25,267 --> 00:16:27,367
and she's the first leader
I've had

339
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:29,333
who didn't make it
about herself.

340
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,400
I'm so sorry.

341
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,333
Excuse me.

342
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:47,000
[NOA EXHALES SHARPLY]

343
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,733
[NOA] You all did
everything you could.

344
00:16:52,467 --> 00:16:53,733
But this is on me.

345
00:16:56,367 --> 00:16:57,733
Go home.

346
00:16:59,433 --> 00:17:01,000
You deserve some rest.

347
00:17:02,767 --> 00:17:04,100
Please.

348
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,400
- Noa.
- Boss.

349
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:09,767
Let's give her
a second to breathe.

350
00:17:09,767 --> 00:17:16,733
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:17:26,367 --> 00:17:31,367
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:17:31,367 --> 00:17:32,500
[PLATE BREAKS]

353
00:17:37,133 --> 00:17:38,267
[TESS] Witch!

354
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:43,533
I've been a nurse in LA
for 30 years.

355
00:17:43,533 --> 00:17:47,533
Meth heads, crackheads,
spoiled Hollywood nepo babies.

356
00:17:47,533 --> 00:17:50,333
Do you really think
I'm scared of you?

357
00:17:51,167 --> 00:17:54,500
I know why
you can't drag me out.

358
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:58,800
You need me to
walk away on my own.

359
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:01,800
But my God gives me that choice.

360
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:02,767
[YOLANDA] Hm.

361
00:18:02,767 --> 00:18:04,600
You think you know better?

362
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:07,133
I'm an Archangel.

363
00:18:07,133 --> 00:18:09,733
So was Lucifer!

364
00:18:10,533 --> 00:18:13,700
Take one step, Tess!

365
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:16,367
And I'll make sure
you regret it.

366
00:18:16,367 --> 00:18:23,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

367
00:18:32,567 --> 00:18:34,367
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

368
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:38,233
You're not giving up, are you?

369
00:18:38,233 --> 00:18:39,700
Oh, I don't have time for this.

370
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:41,700
- Just sit. One second, Noa.
- I have to go.

371
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:44,267
- One second, Noa. Noa, Noa!
- Give me my stuff back!

372
00:18:45,867 --> 00:18:48,467
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

373
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:49,767
What was that?

374
00:18:49,767 --> 00:18:51,733
Ugh, I don't know.

375
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,167
[NOA SIGHS]

376
00:18:56,167 --> 00:18:57,233
It's pretty weak.

377
00:18:57,233 --> 00:18:58,533
Just like that punch.

378
00:19:02,867 --> 00:19:05,700
Arthur, really?

379
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:07,033
I mean, you think he has

380
00:19:07,033 --> 00:19:09,600
the brain capacity for
that information?

381
00:19:10,567 --> 00:19:11,800
I don't know.

382
00:19:12,233 --> 00:19:14,467
Not knowing things just
makes me feel like...

383
00:19:14,467 --> 00:19:15,700
Pissed.

384
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:19,100
I don't want to think
about anything tonight.

385
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:23,767
You don't have to.

386
00:19:26,867 --> 00:19:29,467
Well, at least you have
a girlfriend to go home to.

387
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:30,633
Actually...

388
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:33,367
we broke up.

389
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:38,400
She felt tired of
having to compete.

390
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:42,333
[NOA GASPS]

391
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:45,600
- Oh, I'm so sorry.
- Don't be.

392
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:47,367
I'm fired, anyway.

393
00:19:47,867 --> 00:19:51,467
[TESS] Jesus Christ!
Ew! Why him?

394
00:19:51,467 --> 00:19:53,433
I don't like your pairing.

395
00:19:53,633 --> 00:19:56,467
I'm sorry. Did I do something?

396
00:19:56,467 --> 00:19:58,833
George, that wasn't
supposed to happen.

397
00:19:59,233 --> 00:20:00,500
Um...

398
00:20:00,933 --> 00:20:02,800
Do you know what
I've been through today?

399
00:20:02,833 --> 00:20:04,400
You? Really?

400
00:20:04,667 --> 00:20:05,833
Noa, who are you talking to?

401
00:20:05,833 --> 00:20:06,967
George, can you please get out?

402
00:20:06,967 --> 00:20:08,933
- But I--
- George, please!

403
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:12,533
[NOA SCOFFS]

404
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,900
You have a lot of
explaining to do.

405
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:16,500
Where have you been?

406
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:19,633
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

407
00:20:19,633 --> 00:20:22,600
Tess, you're coming with me!

408
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:24,600
What are you?

409
00:20:27,733 --> 00:20:30,867
You selfish little girl!

410
00:20:30,867 --> 00:20:33,233
You're the reason she insists on

411
00:20:33,233 --> 00:20:35,600
staying where
she doesn't belong.

412
00:20:35,833 --> 00:20:38,567
Please! Stop!

413
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,333
No!

414
00:20:40,333 --> 00:20:41,933
Get off her!

415
00:20:42,433 --> 00:20:43,533
Please!

416
00:20:44,967 --> 00:20:46,833
She's all I have!

417
00:20:46,833 --> 00:20:48,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

418
00:20:48,967 --> 00:20:50,933
All you have.

419
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:53,633
Oh!

420
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:55,733
You don't know.

421
00:20:55,733 --> 00:20:56,867
Don't!

422
00:20:57,633 --> 00:20:58,767
Don't!

423
00:20:59,733 --> 00:21:01,867
She's not all you have!

424
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:05,400
What about your daddy?

425
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:11,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

426
00:21:11,267 --> 00:21:15,400
You don't know
about Pacoima, do you?

427
00:21:17,267 --> 00:21:18,633
[TESS] Dear!

428
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,800
I'm sorry!

429
00:21:24,333 --> 00:21:25,967
I'm sorry.

430
00:21:25,967 --> 00:21:32,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
